17 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a line graph where increasing coupling constant J raises the transient entanglement peak, with curves labeled low J and high J. Panel b features a line graph demonstrating that lower dissipation gamma extends the coherence window, showing higher and lower gamma with an arrow indicating a longer half-life for lower dissipation. Panel c presents a radar chart comparing diagnostic profiles\204memory envelope, collective, and combined\204across peak concurrence, mutual information, half-life, and final purity, with combined showing balanced attributes. Panel d displays a flowchart labeled hypothetical test sequence, linking spin-chain levers, perturbation classes, microtubule readouts, and a decision point to falsify or refine, illustrating an experimental workflow.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Infographic outlining a three-stage experimental escalation protocol: Stage 1 involves in vitro or ex vivo preparations and optical readouts, proceeding only with reproducible shifts; Stage 2 covers animal studies, focusing on EEG and microtubule optics, requiring convergence with control-resistant effects; Stage 3 includes human pilot studies emphasizing safety and non-cognitive outcomes with indirect interpretation. A falsification gate lists stop criteria such as reproducibility failure, classical explanations, negative blinded replication, or loss of optical signatures, with a primary rule halting escalation if Stage 1 results are negative.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
